  "verbalization": "Ixerisoside A is shown to have targets that ultimately lead to C8166 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Ixerisoside A interacts with SK-MEL-28, a melanoma cell line, which is targeted by 2-(5-Hydroxy-1H-Indol-3-Yl)Acetic Acid, a compound that itself targets C8166. Similarly, Ixerisoside A is also shown to interact with Endothelial lipase and Phenylalanine-4-hydroxylase, both of which are targeted by complex molecules that also lead to C8166. These findings collectively indicate that Ixerisoside A may exert its biological effects through multiple pathways, ultimately influencing C8166. The evidence is consistent across different targets, suggesting a potential role for Ixerisoside A in modulating pathways that are involved in the regulation of C8166. The strength of the evidence is moderate, as the scores are relatively low, but the consistency of the targets across different pathways supports a plausible mechanism. The exact nature of the interaction between Ixerisoside A and C8166 remains uncertain, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the proposed relationship.",
